cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mllabiome in research, please cite this software release using these metadata."
title: "mllabiome"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-05
authors:
  - name: "Agata Polejowska"
abstract: >-
  mllabiome is a Python library for leakage-controlled machine learning on
  microbiome data. It supports nested and subject-aware cross-validation,
  leave-one-dataset-out evaluation, microbiota profile data representation
  (MPDR) analysis, base and ensemble microbiota profile modelling algorithms
  (MPMA-B and MPMA-E), multimodal modelling, explainable AI, robustness
  analysis, statistical comparison, and research reporting. It is intended for research use only
  and is not a medical device or clinical decision-support system.
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/CMG-GUTS/mllabiome"
url: "https://github.com/CMG-GUTS/mllabiome"
keywords:
  - microbiome
  - microbiota
  - metagenomics
  - machine learning
  - microbiome machine learning
  - nested cross-validation
  - grouped cross-validation
  - leave-one-dataset-out
  - cross-cohort validation
  - compositional data
  - ensemble learning
  - multimodal learning
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - LIME
  - bioinformatics